        "content": "• Service Positioning: After a side out, the first serve is determined by the team's\nscore: the player on the right (baseline facing the net) serves if the score is even, and\nthe player on the left serves if the score is odd.\n\n• Switching Sides: Players only switch sides after winning a point on their own serve.\nThe same player continues serving from the new side.\n\n• Side Outs & Scoring: If the serving team loses a rally, a side out occurs; the\nopposing team earns a point and takes over the serve.\n\n• Game Points: A team can win a point regardless of whether they are serving or\nreceiving except for the winning point (see next item).\n\n• Scoring Freeze and Match Point: To keep the game competitive through the final\npoint, a scoring freeze shall take eƯect whenever a team reaches one point below\nthe game-winning score. Once a team reaches the freeze point, it may score the\ngame-winning point only while serving. For example, in a game played to 25 points,\na team’s score shall initially freeze at 24. The scoring freeze applies only to the team\nthat has reached the freeze point; the opposing team may continue to score using\nnormal Rally Scoring until it also reaches the applicable freeze point. A team must\nbe serving to score the game-winning point.\n\n• Win-by-Two (2) Games: When the game is played using a win-by-two (2) format\nand the score becomes tied at or beyond the initial freeze point, neither team can\nwin by scoring the next point. Therefore, both teams’ scores shall become\nunfrozen, and normal Rally Scoring shall resume. Thereafter, a team’s score shall\nfreeze again whenever it reaches a score at which its next point would win the"
